<h2 id="what-is-aweber">📧 What Is AWeber?</h2>

AWeber launched in 1998, making it one of the oldest email marketing platforms still actively serving businesses today. While newer competitors chase AI-powered everything, AWeber has steadily evolved its core offering: dependable email delivery with enough automation to run serious D2C operations.

The platform targets small to mid-sized businesses, though we've seen it scale effectively for brands pushing 200K+ subscribers. AWeber handles the essentials well—broadcast emails, automated sequences, landing pages, and basic segmentation—without overwhelming operators with features they'll never touch.

For D2C specifically, AWeber integrates with Shopify, WooCommerce, BigCommerce, and most major ecommerce platforms. The integrations aren't as deep as purpose-built ecommerce email tools like Klaviyo, but they're functional enough for most use cases.

